 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Dmitry Nagiyev proudly explains that the banquet is for the film crew of his new comedy, and the moment he leaves the kitchen, Senya begins roasting modern Russian cinema.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "А что за банкет сегодня?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Кино со мной закончили снимать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я там в главной роли.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Комедия правда очень смешная.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Давайте не отвлекаемся от работы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Салаты и закуски готовим быстро.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ну всё понятно с этим кино.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Опять сняли какую-то ерунду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "И она всю кассу соберёт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Ещё кто-то так думает?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это кино окупается до выхода.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Туда просто рекламу напихают.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's break down each line as Nagiyev brags and Senya critiques the film industry.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "А что за банкет сегодня?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And what kind of banquet is it today?' The conversational question phrase 'what for a banquet' asks what the occasion is.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Кино со мной закончили снимать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They finished filming a movie with me.' In everyday Russian, 'cinema, movies' flows straight into 'to take off, peel' without extra linking words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я там в главной роли.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I have the lead role in it.' Nagiyev pairs 'main, most important' with 'role, part' directly, since spoken Russian skips English filler words like 'the', 'a', and 'is'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Комедия правда очень смешная.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The comedy is truly very funny.' Used as an adverb, the noun for 'truth' means 'truly' or 'really'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Давайте не отвлекаемся от работы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let's not get distracted from work.' Starting with the everyday word for 'let us' is how Russian speakers warmly invite someone to do something together.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Салаты и закуски готовим быстро.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We prepare the salads and appetizers quickly.' Plural direct objects precede the first-person plural verb for a brisk kitchen order.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ну всё понятно с этим кино.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, everything is clear with this movie.' The neuter predicative word for 'understandable' sums up Senya's cynical verdict.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Опять сняли какую-то ерунду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They filmed some nonsense again.' In cinema, the verb for 'to take off' or 'photograph' also means 'to shoot a film'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "И она всю кассу соберёт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And it will collect the whole box office.' Literally 'will gather the whole cash register', this idiom means a movie will make a fortune at the box office.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Ещё кто-то так думает?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Does anyone else think so?' Combining 'still/more' with 'someone' creates the meaning 'anyone else'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это кино окупается до выхода.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This movie pays for itself before release.' Senya pairs 'cinema, movies' with 'exit; way out' directly, since spoken Russian skips English filler words like 'the', 'a', and 'is'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Туда просто рекламу напихают.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They just cram commercials into it.' Russian uses a singular collective noun for 'advertising' or 'commercials'. Now let's hear the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "А что за банкет сегодня?",
